Patch 0084: the EE scheduler's run loop does less per dispatch.

What it fixes: measured (work/perf-review/report.md, section 1), EeScheduler::run and the lookup of the
next function cost more than the game's own code. Three changes, none of which alters guest state:
  1. publishDebugContext (four relaxed stores of pc, ra, sp, gp into PS2Runtime::m_debugPc/Ra/Sp/Gp) ran on
     every iteration. Its readers are the debug panel (ps2EntryRunner only, not built by this port) and
     aggressive-log lines; no guest-visible state reads it. It now runs only when DON_EE_DEBUG_CONTEXT=1
     (read once). The idle and state-change publishes are untouched.
  2. PS2Runtime::findFunction is an out-of-line call that did the same range check and load the dispatch
     fast path does. The run loop now does it inline against the same dense table
     (g_ps2RecompiledFunctionTable, already indexed by (pc - base) >> 2, which covers the code range), so
     replaceFunction'd entries win exactly as before; same dispatch-history push when enabled.
  3. ps2IsNativeFunction was already behind the cheap pc == entryPc && !m_unwinding tests; left as is
     (it is a semantic guard of patch 0055, not a diagnostic).
Same order of events and same cycle charges: no accounting call was moved or added.

Verified: the file compiles with the project's flags; the integrator checks the 4-player state hash.
Based on no other project.

